The 1917–18 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 30th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1910/celtic1918.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1917-18|website=Londonhearts.com|accessdate=2 April 2019}}</ref> After having won the previous four championships, they narrowly failed to defend their league title as they finished runners-up just one point below [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]]. Both teams were tied on points on the last day, but Celtic drew home to [[Motherwell F.C.|Motherwell]], 1-1; and Rangers won 2–1 home against [[Clyde F.C.|Clyde]].

For the fourth consecutive season, the Scottish Cup remained suspended because of [[World War I]], so Celtic remained title-holders.

Celtic won the [[Glasgow Charity Cup|Glasgow Merchants' Charity Cup]] for the seventh season in a row.

